	chapter.42AAA7B01C137071.title: "Way to One's Heart"
	chapter.4CFC48351FFEBA69.title: "Gotta Catch 'Em All"
	chapter.52733FFDCBB4B73A.title: "PLEASE READ FIRST!"
	chapter.68B3A5035649D825.title: "Landmarks of the World"
	chapter.69A1664BDAEAA81F.title: "Storage Solutions"
	chapter.7105AFDC71F81465.title: "Useful Information"
	chapter_group.6AC07E42885B0D55.title: "Main Quests"
	file.0000000000000001.title: "Fid's Cobblemon Event"
	quest.00ADD2809FC49F4A.title: "Midas Gold Armory"
	quest.011F00CF8259AFD1.quest_desc: [
		"There are many floral wonders in the world of Cobblemon--many different &l&2berries&r&r and other crops are out there with their own benefits. Why not forage for these berries and build a big garden? It'll certainly do you and your Pokemon some good!"
		""
		"Certain berry trees spawn in specific biomes, while some are acquired from Pokemon only. Go forth, collect, and cultivate as many different berries as possible!"
	]
	quest.0153D59387F6A20C.quest_desc: [
		"Starting off on your Pokemon adventures, you'll soon find that your Pokemon will run out of &l&ePP&r&r real quickly and can no longer use their best moves. So what do you do to replenish it?"
		""
		"You can go to sleep, but in order for night to pass, a &opercentage of players&r in the server will have to do the same."
		""
		"[ \"The better way before you get a Healing Machine is to mutate Oran berries to get Leppa berries. You can find more about mutating \", { \"text\": \"HERE\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"202DA85A2682E350\" } }, \".\" ]"
	]
	quest.0153D59387F6A20C.title: "No PP??"
	quest.018D46ADBF61295D.title: "Carmot Armory"
	quest.019937E1B4E453C7.quest_desc: [
		"The &lRestoration Tank&r is part of a series of 3 blocks needed to assemble the &zRestoration Machine&r. Put all three in the same formation as shown in the quest bubbles, with the Restoration Tank on the right and the Analyzer and Data Monitor stacked on each other."
		""
		"The Restoration Tank is where the embryo of the fossil grows. It requires &oorganic material&r to fill it up and be a suitable environment for the embryo to grow."
	]
	quest.01CE5ECBDAF15734.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Belue and Coba."]
	quest.01CE5ECBDAF15734.title: "Rowap Berry"
	quest.02B63C9A9D5842E9.quest_desc: [
		"A &lTotem of Undying&r is a single-use item in Minecraft that prevents a player from dying once when held in their hand or off-hand."
		""
		"When fatal damage is taken, it activates, granting effects like &oregeneration&r, &ofire resistance&r, and &oabsorption&r, while the totem is consumed"
	]
	quest.0309CA9430B67D28.quest_desc: ["Gather some souvenirs from the &l&0Deep Dark&r&r, if you can survive the trip..."]
	quest.0309CA9430B67D28.title: "Sculkin' Around"
	quest.03437405A79E3294.quest_desc: ["&l&6Bronze&r&r is an alloy of &ocopper&r and &otin&r. As such, it is an improved metal, slightly better than iron!"]
	quest.03437405A79E3294.title: "Bronze"
	quest.0364E586278B5A86.quest_desc: [
		"&lAprijuice&r is an item that modifies the riding stats of a Pokémon. Aprijuice can be cooked from any of the seven apricorn colors along with a Pep-Up Flower, an Energy Root, and any combination of berries. The &zcolor&r of the apricorn used changes the base attribute boost:"
		""
		"&4Red Aprijuice&r - +2 Acceleration, -1 Stamina"
		"&eYellow Aprijuice&r - +2 Stamina, -1 Skill"
		"&9Blue Aprijuice&r - +2 Skill, -1 Jump"
		"&2Green Aprijuice&r - +2 Jump, -1 Speed"
		"&dPink Aprijuice&r - +2 Speed, -1 Acceleration"
		"&0Black Aprijuice&r - No extra attribute boost"
		"White Aprijuice - -2 in all ride attributes"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The taste of certain berries correlate with riding stats."
		""
		"&cAcceleration&r = &cSpicy&r"
		"&eStamina&r = &eSour&r"
		"&9Skill&r = &9Dry&r"
		"&aJump&r = &aBitter&r"
		"&dSpeed&r = &dSweet&r"
		""
		"Add berries as seasoning carefully!"
	]
	quest.0364E586278B5A86.title: "Aprijuice"
	quest.03EA05AE42175754.quest_desc: [
		"A &l&2mint leaf&r&r is an item used to craft mints and are obtained by harvesting the final stage of a mint crop, which produces 1-3 of the respective mint leaf. If the plant is not fully mature, it will only drop seeds."
		""
		"Mint leaves do not have a favored biome and can spawn anywhere on the surface of the Overworld."
		""
		"A total of four mint leaves can be combined to create a full Mint which can change the &lNature&r of your Pokemon."
	]
	quest.03EA05AE42175754.title: "Minty Fresh"
	quest.045CFE202D4940CA.quest_desc: [
		"A &lPasture Block&r is a utility block that allows the player to deposit Pokémon from their PC into the surrounding area."
		""
		"The main purpose of the pasture block is to allow players to let out their Pokémon into a set area, being able to be interacted as if they were wild or thrown out of their ball."
		""
		"Pressing use on a pasture block opens the GUI of the player's PC."
		""
		"A pasture block can hold up to 16 Pokémon."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To &lBreed&r your Pokemon, you'll need this block. Place your Pokemon to roam in the pasture, click the button to activate breeding, and come back later to maybe find an egg in the nesting area on the bottom of the pasture block!"
	]
	quest.045CFE202D4940CA.title: "Pasture Blocks and Breeding"
	quest.059DFD738EC0970B.title: "Tidesinger Armory"
	quest.05B10B0A6B8D5B42.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Touga and Occa."]
	quest.05B10B0A6B8D5B42.title: "Tamato Berry"
	quest.05B6B045D15CE269.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Persim and Cheri."]
	quest.05B6B045D15CE269.title: "Figy Berry"
	quest.05CC094A7B604DAD.quest_desc: ["Your reward for defeating the Wither is a &zNether Star&r, which can be used to craft a number of powerful items."]
	quest.05DC390697EBFAB2.quest_desc: ["&lSport Balls&r are equivalent to Great Balls, having a 1.5x catch rate bonus."]
	quest.0665A3A34B54EBFC.quest_desc: [
		"What if you want your inventories to be organized in separate spaces instead of all hugging the terminal?"
		""
		"Create some &l&2Inventory Cables&r&r and connect them to &lInventory Cable Connectors&r attached to your storage."
	]
	quest.06FE957AE51AD9FC.title: "Steel Armory"
	quest.07378EB5AE7CC844.quest_desc: ["These are &lframed&r versions of Inventory Cables and Connectors. You can \"paint\" these to take up a block texture to make your setup look even neater!"]
	quest.07877392BAB79647.quest_desc: [
		"&lConduits&r are powerful items that give the &bConduit Power&r AoE effect when players are in contact with rain or water."
		""
		"This effect restores oxygen, gives underwater night vision and increases mining speed by 16.7% (1/6th)."
		""
		"Conduits also damage any hostile mobs, like drowned, guardians, and elder guardians, within a range of 8 blocks of the conduit."
		""
		"Conduits can be activated in &oany&r biome and at any height or depth."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In order for the conduit to be active, it has to be in the center of a 3x3x3 volume of water which itself must be enclosed within an activation frame."
		""
		"The frame is built out of blocks in &lthree 5×5 open squares&r centered on the conduit, one around each axis."
		""
		"Only prismarine, dark prismarine, prismarine bricks, and sea lantern blocks in the frame contribute to activation."
		""
		"A minimum of &o16 blocks&r are required and produce an effective range of 32 blocks."
	]
	quest.0791550550B3C1A6.quest_desc: ["&lLuxury Balls&r don't have an improved catch rate bonus, but any Pokemon caught with them will gain Friendship twice as fast!"]
	quest.085DC4D1AF85B481.quest_desc: ["&lFast Balls&r have a 4x Catch Rate bonus vs Pokemon with a base speed 100 or above!"]
	quest.08EBC8B4461F2DDC.quest_desc: ["You can fly on your Pokemon, but what if you wanted to fly on your own? The &lElytra&r is still there, waiting for you in the End Ships..."]
	quest.09E180E0A9E68CD5.quest_desc: ["&l&0Durasteel&r&r is a superior form of Steel acquired from smelting &5Manganese&r and &#1B8D55Quadrillum&r&r."]
	quest.09E180E0A9E68CD5.title: "Durasteel"
	quest.0A1383D67C585ED2.title: "Silver Armory"
	quest.0A1C83F15DEDA31A.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Nomel and Payapa."]
	quest.0A1C83F15DEDA31A.title: "Belue Berry"
	quest.0AF1B8B47C259734.quest_desc: [
		"The &lAdvanced Wireless Terminal&r is better than the other one in every way. You can bind your Wireless Terminal to a set Terminal by &4shift+right-clicking&r it."
		""
		"It works from &o64 blocks away&r (4 chunks length), and you can also greatly increase the range by putting a Beacon near your set Terminal."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A &lLevel 1&r Beacon will extend the range to anywhere in the set terminal's dimension (make sure you chunkload the set terminal)."
		""
		"A &lLevel 4&r Beacon will allow you to access your terminal &zcross-dimensionally&r!"
	]
	quest.0B10020B7FCC4C39.quest_desc: [
		"&#FFEAB8&lHallowed Ingots&r&r can be acquired by smelting Orichalcum, Mythril, and Adamantine ores in a Level 2 Alloy Forge."
		""
		"Hallowed Armor has an incredible amount of &oToughness&r, and will make you look truly regal."
		""
		"Hallowed Ingots are also needed to create the &#FFEAB8&lSword of Aegis&r."
	]
	quest.0EA458C9D39BF555.quest_desc: ["Take to the skies and fetch me 10 Flying types!"]
	quest.0EE8C9716B5ED191.quest_desc: [
		"An &2&lapricorn tree&r&r is a type of tree that can rarely be found in &lany&r biome."
		""
		"All apricorn trees generate with a single type of apricorn, of which it will have an indeterminate amount growing on it."
		""
		"Interact with the apricorns growing off the leaves in order to harvest them."
	]
	quest.0EE8C9716B5ED191.title: "The Shell of the Pokeball"
	quest.0EFEE87C72270F80.quest_desc: ["The &lWireless Terminal&r lets you access your terminal from afar. &4Right-click&r on the terminal you want to connect to with the Wireless Terminal in hand. This specific device will work &o16 blocks&r away."]
	quest.10065466E72861FD.quest_desc: [
		"These special wands will allow you to set down a multiple amount of blocks at once and in different orientations."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nModes:&r&r"
		""
		"- Directional Mode: Single block placement in 9 directions from a block."
		""
		"- Row/Column mode: Multiple blocks at once in a row or column, press &l&4X&r&r to change orientation."
		""
		"- Fill mode: Fill between 2 corners, same block, or random."
		""
		"- Area mode: Fill connected blocks, like making an X-shaped plank structure thicker!"
		""
		"- Grid mode: Fixed 2d grid, use arrow keys or gui to change size."
		""
		"- Line mode: Line from block to block."
		""
		"- Circle mode: Circle from center block to radius block (press &l&4K&r&r to change to a filled circle)."
		""
		"- Copy mode: Copy between corners."
		""
		"- Paste mode: Paste previously copied blocks, press &l&4R&r&r to cycle rotation on Y axis by 90 degrees increments."
		""
		"- Blast mode: Destroy blocks with an explosion. In survival the player needs TNT in their inventory."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are a number of wands, all with different block limits."
		""
		"- Stone wand: &l16&r block limit."
		"- Iron wand: &l32&r block limit."
		"- Diamond wand: &l64&r block limit."
		"- Netherite wand: &l256&r block limit."
	]
	quest.10065466E72861FD.title: "Builder's Wands"
	quest.10400839D85AA87F.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Dripstone, Mountain, Sandy, or Volcanic biomes."]
	quest.10400839D85AA87F.title: "Charti Berry"
	quest.106FC22647A1B0E0.quest_desc: ["&lHeavy Balls&r have an effective catch bonus range of 1x to 4x, going up the heavier the enemy Pokemon!"]
	quest.10C5B76C07E0FC78.quest_desc: ["&l&bRunite&r&r is a powerful metal that can be found in two spawn ranges: Y 39-53, and Y -55-37. It needs iron tools or greater to mine."]
	quest.10C5B76C07E0FC78.title: "Runite"
	quest.1139A56637D270F0.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Figy and Razz."]
	quest.1139A56637D270F0.title: "Touga Berry"
	quest.11D52E82D019C3AE.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2Waystones&r&r allow you teleportation from one Waystone to another in the world, and even across dimensions!"
		""
		"You can craft them or find Waystones in villages. Once the Abyss Watcher upon the pedestal is activated, the Waystone will be added to your list of Waystones to teleport in between."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nAbyss Watcher&r&r"
		""
		"{image:fwaystones:item/abyss_watcher width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Used for crafting the waystones, as well as teleporting to other waystones by right clicking it, consuming the item upon use."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nEmpty Waystone Scroll&r&r"
		""
		"{image:fwaystones:item/empty_waystone_scroll width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Used for storing all your discovered waystones in it. Using the filled waystone scroll will discover all the stored waystones to the player using it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nLocal Void&r&r"
		""
		"{image:fwaystones:item/local_void_inert width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Right clicking on a waystone will bind it to that waystone. Right clicking anywhere else will teleport the player to the bound location, as long as it exists, free of charge (configurable), with the item disappearing on use (configurable). The item can be reset by shift-right clicking."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nPocket Wormhole&r&r"
		""
		"{image:fwaystones:item/pocket_wormhole width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Similarly to the Abyss Watcher, it allows the players to open the teleportation interface from anywhere, except the item doesn't get destroyed on teleportation."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nVoid Totem&r&r"
		""
		"{image:fwaystones:item/void_totem width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Just like the Local Void, the Void Totem can be bound to a Waystone. If you die with a bound one equipped, it will teleport you to the bound Waystone. Should it be unbound, it will choose a random one you have discovered. Otherwise, it simply acts like a normal Totem of Undying."
	]
	quest.11D52E82D019C3AE.title: "Waystones"
	quest.11DB1A13714DAFCF.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Oran and one of the following: Razz, Bluk, Nanab, Wepear, or Pinap."]
	quest.11DB1A13714DAFCF.title: "Leppa Berry"
	quest.1279FD428AD99391.quest_desc: [
		"&lBanglum&r ore can be found in a depth of Y 48-69 and should be mined with iron tools."
		""
		"Rarely when mining this ore, you can get a &l&2Banglum Chunk&r&r. This can be used to upgrade Banglum equipment to &l&eLegendary variants&r&r, which give them a range of perks!"
		""
		"&oNether Banglum ore&r drops chunks far more often than the stone variant."
		""
		"This is a very &l&4volatile&r&r ore which can explode, more often in the Nether. A tool with &oSilk Touch&r will greatly lessen the chance of this happening."
	]
	quest.1279FD428AD99391.title: "Banglum"
	quest.1297DF4F4049A8F8.quest_desc: [
		"There are a number of &lrenowned regional dishes&r that you can cook yourself!"
		""
		"Gather different food items and ingredients and you'll be sure to formulate some recipes for the &oCampfire Pot&r!"
	]
	quest.1297DF4F4049A8F8.title: "Delicacies around the Globe"
	quest.12CFB1DA31A20E04.quest_desc: [
		"Inventory Profiles Next is a mod that helps keep your inventory organized and sorted."
		""
		"&l&nSorting:&r&r"
		""
		"Pressing &l&4R&r&r will automatically sort your inventory. There is a \"Z\" button in the UI that can also sort things."
		""
		"There are other buttons that can also sort things by rows or columns."
		""
		"You can go into the mod's config menu for many other sorting methods that you can modify."
		""
		"&l&nCrafting:&r&r"
		""
		"You can enable &lautocrafting&r by clicking the box next to the crafting grid. If you &l&4alt-click&r&r on the output item, it brings all the ingredients into the crafting grid as a &ofull stack&r."
		""
		"&l&4Shift+alt and clicking&r&r will go through every stack in your inventory to make the output item."
	]
	quest.1326AA6E869391F5.title: "Prometheum Armory"
	quest.136C2644F5E3208B.title: "Aquarium Armory"
	quest.13E291211614CDB8.quest_desc: [
		"The &lData Monitor&r is part of a series of 3 blocks needed to assemble the &zRestoration Machine&r. Put all three in the same formation as shown in the quest bubbles, with the Restoration Tank on the right and the Analyzer and Data Monitor stacked on each other."
		""
		"The Data Monitor shows the progress of the embryo's growth."
	]
	quest.13F05FC3A7B0A2BE.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Sitrus and Haban."]
	quest.13F05FC3A7B0A2BE.title: "Pomeg Berry"
	quest.13FFABBC8A5A24BD.quest_desc: ["The &lLove Ball&r has a 2.5x catch rate bonus if the enemy Pokemon's gender is opposite yours. The catch rate rockets up to 8x if they're the same species!"]
	quest.14040081429A2C17.quest_desc: [
		"&lWelcome to the world of Cobblemon!&r"
		""
		"In this world, biomes are very &lexpansive&r and &lsprawling&r, fitting for the new age of &o&erideable Pokemon&r&r! Many treasures await you out there, better get going!"
	]
	quest.1440B4A115E6ACB8.quest_desc: ["The &lCarmot Bell&r is a special placeable tool that gives off a &2healing aura&r to anyone near it."]
	quest.1444F8E8000160FB.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Forest, Jungle, or Swamp biomes."]
	quest.1444F8E8000160FB.title: "Tanga Berry"
	quest.14BB110FA2CC440A.quest_desc: [
		"How do we connect &omultiple chests&r to actually make a storage system? The &l&6Inventory Connector Block&r&r should be placed behind the Terminal you're using. You can then put inventory blocks like chests &oadjacent&r to that Inventory Connector. Everything will show up in your Terminal now!"
		""
		"&oEven better:&r You can stack double chests on each other, horizontally or vertically, and as long as one is touching the Inventory Connector, all contents will still show up!"
	]
	quest.14C378BB68E4B8C3.quest_desc: [
		"The &lTrident&r is a magnificent weapon that can be thrown. It has a number of its own enchantments too."
		""
		"You can get a trident as a rare drop from trident-wielding Drowned mobs, get it from trial vaults, or even craft them with &9Aquarium Pearls&r."
	]
	quest.14F5BF551B9632DC.quest_desc: ["The &lHeal Ball&r fully heals a Pokemon caught by it."]
	quest.153FC04034645E77.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Pamtre and Kelpsy."]
	quest.153FC04034645E77.title: "Liechi Berry"
	quest.15C38E4B51C059B7.quest_desc: ["Catch me 10 Normal Types and I'll give you some coins!"]
	quest.15C686082A1BF122.quest_desc: ["&lTimer Balls'&r effectiveness increases up to 4x depending on how many turns passed in battle, with the max turns at 10."]
	quest.16875785F44378F2.quest_desc: [
		"&l&nNature's Compass:&r&r"
		""
		"The &l&2Nature's Compass&r&r is a utility item that allows you to search for a biome's location anywhere in the world and view information about it. If you're looking for a compass to locate structures, check out Explorer's Compass."
		""
		"- &l&4Right-clicking&r&r with Nature's Compass in hand will open the biome selection GUI, from which you can search for a biome or view information about it."
		""
		"- &l&4Shift-right-clicking&r&r will reset the compass's state."
		""
		"- When the compass is not pointing at a biome, it will point at the world spawn."
	]
	quest.175B72CB4D34DB18.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Mountain biomes."]
	quest.175B72CB4D34DB18.title: "Aspear Berry"
	quest.17C90C8FEF38A47C.title: "Durasteel Tools"
	quest.184589CCF1A4DD74.quest_desc: ["Let the sparks fly as you catch 10 electrifying Pokemon!"]
	quest.19DF3C1711E7E3B9.title: "Carmot Tools"
	quest.1A16EEA020043B2D.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Forest biomes."]
	quest.1A16EEA020043B2D.title: "Chesto Berry"
	quest.1A3998AA77D42016.title: "Fishing Boats"
	quest.1A57445DD4CC44BC.quest_desc: ["&lPark Balls&r have a catch rate bonus of 2.5x when used in Plains or Forest biomes!"]
	quest.1A8487EF38226A2F.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Lum and Leppa."]
	quest.1A8487EF38226A2F.title: "Hopo Berry"
	quest.1ADB5676E7965302.quest_desc: [
		"&lQuadrillum&r is an ore that can be found in a range of Y 12-40 and requires iron tools to mine."
		""
		"You can make a number of tools with this material, slightly weaker than diamond tools, but you can also smelt it with &l&dManganese&r&r to get &l&0Durasteel&r&r!"
	]
	quest.1ADB5676E7965302.title: "Quadrillum"
	quest.1B18E77AC18EBDE8.quest_desc: [
		"The &lAegis Smithing Template&r is one that can only be found held by a &oMaster cleric villager&r. "
		""
		"This template helps get you two types of Aegis blades: The &l&4Blade of Aegis&r&r, and the &#FFEAB8&lSword of Aegis&r, which are acquired from the Palladium Sword and Hallowed Sword respectively."
	]
	quest.1B18E77AC18EBDE8.title: "Aegis Smithing Template"
	quest.1B66388A59A28505.quest_desc: ["&lQuick Balls&r have a staggering 5x catch rate bonus on the first turn of battle ONLY!"]
	quest.1C12AFB6B6582C73.quest_desc: ["Test your might and spirit, and catch me 10 Fighting type Pokemon!"]
	quest.1C500F817F6E37CC.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Rabuta and Shuca."]
	quest.1C500F817F6E37CC.title: "Hondew Berry"
	quest.1CD89B416065F26D.title: "Legendary Banglum Armory"
	quest.1D62DFB91DFC7877.title: "Star Platinum Tools"
	quest.1DCD90916CCBBB63.quest_desc: ["&lNest Balls&r have a catch rate bonus range of 1x-4x, depending on how much lower the Pokemon's level is from 30."]
	quest.1E8FACE73FD26326.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Lum with one of the following: Figy, Wiki, Mago, Aguav, and Iapapa."]
	quest.1E8FACE73FD26326.title: "Sitrus Berry"
	quest.1EBB04053FFDEB13.quest_desc: ["You make a &lRevive&r, you'll need to cook a &oHeal Powder&r and &oHoney Bottle&r together in a Campfire Pot. To get a &2Heal Powder&r, you can craft it directly from &lRevival Herbs&r."]
	quest.1F2E2BC4889AA0B7.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Belue and Grepa."]
	quest.1F2E2BC4889AA0B7.title: "Apicot Berry"
	quest.200C7D3620893B84.quest_desc: [
		"&l&dPlatinum&r&r is a metal that can be found in spawn range Y 8-32 and can be mined with iron tools."
		""
		"It can be smelted with &lStarrite&r&r to get &l&5Star Platinum&r&r. Even better, it is a vital component in making &zCelestial metal&r."
	]
	quest.200C7D3620893B84.title: "Platinum"
	quest.202DA85A2682E350.quest_desc: [
		"Players can engage in more advanced berry farming by planting specific berry trees &ladjacent&r—&4but not diagonally&r—to each other for a chance to harvest mutated berries."
		""
		"Each harvest provides a &l12.5%&r chance for a berry tree to yield &2mutated berries&r instead of normal ones. This chance can be increased through the use of &lSurprise Mulch&r."
		""
		"See if you can get a Lum Berry for me!"
	]
	quest.202DA85A2682E350.title: "Mutating Berries"
	quest.207D985608F92D1A.quest_desc: ["These Pokemon will rock your world! Get me 10 of them, stat!"]
	quest.20807923108875E6.title: "Mythril Tools"
	quest.20CD250C6F8B9941.quest_desc: [
		"&l&nVanitySlots&r&r is a mod that adds four extra armor slots to your inventory using the Accessories API. The armor put in these four extra slots are what gets rendered instead of the armor you are actually wearing, meaning you can wear whatever armor you want while still looking stylish."
		""
		"VanitySlots also adds &2four extra pieces of armor&r meant to &lhide&r the armor you're currently wearing. These pieces of armor can be crafted by surrounding leather armor with eight pieces of glowstone dust in a crafting table."
	]
	quest.20DE6C99637D7A62.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Jungle and Swamp biomes."]
	quest.20DE6C99637D7A62.title: "Persim Berry"
	quest.2103163A3DCE124D.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Watmel and Qualot."]
	quest.2103163A3DCE124D.title: "Ganlon Berry"
	quest.2131EBDBAA68381B.quest_desc: [
		"&lFlan&r (originally from Fabric LANd) is a server sided claiming mod that helps you protect your builds in a server from other players."
		""
		"With intuitive GUI and world interactions you can easily create and manage protected regions, and if GUIs are not your flavor ingame commands can replace that too."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nAbout Claims:&r&r"
		"&l&bClaims&r&r are pieces of land with restricted permissions to prevent griefing."
		""
		"By default a claim has a depth of &l10 blocks&r which means they extend 10 blocks downwards from the claiming spot and then extend all the way to build limit. The claim will automatically extend &odownwards&r if the player starts building below it. This system is in place to allow for mining below a claim unlike other claiming mods where you simply hit a \"wall\" when digging."
		""
		"There are other claim types in addition to this:"
		""
		"- Subclaims as the name suggests are a claim within a claim. Subclaims each have their own permission set allowing you to even finer tune the area and what other players are allowed to do."
		""
		"- 3d Claims: Normally claims are 2 dimensional. While they have a depth they extend all the way upwards. You are able to create 3 dimension claims too though which have a fixed dimension."
		"Unlike 2 dimensional ones these will not automatically adjust their size."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nGetting Started:&r&r"
		""
		"To get started the first thing you need is a &l&egolden hoe&r&r. This will be your tool to create land claims."
		""
		"Holding the tool will display your current claim blocks and the amount you used."
		""
		"To &lcreate&r a claim now &l&4right click&r&r on one block to select a corner and on another block to set the other corner. If it was successful you will get a message that a claim was created, else it will tell you why the creation failed."
		""
		"&lResizing&r claim is done by right clicking on one corner of a claim and then on another block to set the new corner. To check if a block is claimed you can use the inspect tool (default is a stick)."
		""
		"Standing in a claim and typing &n/flan menu&r a gui will open to help you customize your claim further."
	]
	quest.2131EBDBAA68381B.title: "FLAN"
	quest.21B9E56D54F5EFDD.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Persim and Pecha."]
	quest.21B9E56D54F5EFDD.title: "Mago Berry"
	quest.221608CB18122C06.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Arid biomes."]
	quest.221608CB18122C06.title: "Rawst Berry"
	quest.221E7931546A9E50.quest_desc: ["The very earth quakes as these Pokemon harness its power! Catch me 10 of them, and try not to get buried!"]
	quest.2221E9E8A83C4FAC.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Pamtre and Kebia."]
	quest.2221E9E8A83C4FAC.title: "Micle Berry"
	quest.222F4DD8AE24C142.quest_desc: ["I can read your mind: You want to catch 10 Psychic types...for 50 shiny coins!"]
	quest.23585E50F5B74161.quest_desc: ["The &l&dStormyx Shield&r&r is the most &odurable&r shield available, and gives further magic protection!"]
	quest.23EF997BDBD64320.quest_desc: [
		"&l&#214EFFMythril&r&r ore can be found at a range of Y -24-4 and requires Diamond tools to mine."
		""
		"On top of being able to make tools and armor with it, you can also create the &l&#214EFFMythril Drill&r&r, a powerful and formidable pickaxe tool that can be upgraded!"
	]
	quest.23EF997BDBD64320.title: "Mythril"
	quest.244E8701B74626F5.title: "Banglum Armory"
	quest.2505BFE592F4A8AB.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Grassland, Hills, and Sky biomes."]
	quest.2505BFE592F4A8AB.title: "Wacan Berry"
	quest.251DE1A00B82F1E4.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Iapapa and Pinap."]
	quest.251DE1A00B82F1E4.title: "Nomel Berry"
	quest.255EB1D61F4F0DDF.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Cornn and Passho."]
	quest.255EB1D61F4F0DDF.title: "Pamtre Berry"
	quest.257A17954E85AECA.quest_desc: [
		"&l&zMetallurgium&r&r can be acquired by smelting together Unobtainium, Adamantine, Orichalcum, Mythril, and Palladium."
		""
		"If you want the absolute &otoughest gear&r ever conceived, the Metallurgium armor set is for you! You will become a true tank to be feared!"
	]
	quest.257A17954E85AECA.title: "Metallurgium"
	quest.25848AFA4F3FBF66.quest_desc: [
		"&lMouse Tweaks&r replaces the standard &l&4RMB&r&r dragging mechanic, adds two new &l&4LMB&r&r dragging mechanics and an ability to quickly move items with the scroll wheel."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nRMB Tweak:&r&r"
		""
		"Very similar to the standard RMB dragging mechanic, with one difference: if you drag over a slot multiple times, an item will be put there multiple times. Replaces the standard mechanic if enabled."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nLMB Tweak (with item):&r&r"
		""
		"Lets you quickly pick up or move items of the same type. Hold &l&4LMB&r&r to pick up an item, then drag it while still holding the item to pick up all similar items in an inventory."
		""
		"You can hold &l&4shift&r&r while dragging to move items of the same type into your inventory."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nLMB Tweak (without item):&r&r"
		""
		"Quickly moves items into another inventory. Hold &l&4shift&r&r, then &l&4LMB&r&r to move items into another inventory."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nWheel Tweak:&r&r"
		""
		"&l&4Scroll&r&r to quickly move items between inventories. When you scroll down on an item stack, its items will be moved one by one. When you scroll up, items will be moved into it from another inventory."
	]
	quest.25BDEEECBA104636.quest_desc: [
		"While your Pokemon is out of its ball, you can give it instructions with the &l&ePoke Staff&r&r."
		""
		"Also, be sure that your favored move for it to use is the first slot in its move list! Yes, different moves have different effects, special moves typically taking the form of a projectile. You'll want to &4avoid&r putting status moves in the first slot."
		""
		"Your Pokemon will automatically attack anything that attacks you, and typically will engage with what you attack initially."
	]
	quest.25BDEEECBA104636.title: "ATTACK!"
	quest.2626F81BD651931F.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Arid or Grasslands biomes."]
	quest.2626F81BD651931F.title: "Shuca Berry"
	quest.266D39EE1910F167.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.266D39EE1910F167.title: "Copper Tools"
	quest.26B8E47B4F4B27D3.title: "Hallowed Tools"
	quest.26E5610267CF519C.quest_desc: ["Truly fearsome, truly powerful! But can you handle 10 Dragons? Then bring 'em to me!"]
	quest.26F5E50CA2C0C1F8.title: "Hidden Bunker Ruins"
	quest.275CB8592A197F09.title: "Runite Armory"
	quest.27B49C3A59E70812.quest_desc: ["Free The End. Kill the Dragon."]
	quest.2848653DFE24A991.quest_desc: ["This powerful &l&2hammer&r&r will mine a space of &o3x3x2&r. Your strip mining ventures will be a lot more tolerable with this instrument in your grasp."]
	quest.28793DC1CB2F1003.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Mountain or Taiga biomes."]
	quest.28793DC1CB2F1003.title: "Bluk Berry"
	quest.287C8B67D59F106A.quest_desc: [
		"&lIV Candies&r can be made to either increase or decrease a Pokemon's &zIVs&r."
		""
		"IV-&2increasing&r candies are made with an EV berry, honeycombs, and an M EXP candy (or greater)."
		""
		"IV-&4decreasing&r candies are made with an EV berry, Enigma berry, and an M EXP candy (or greater)."
		""
		"IVs are Individual Values that further increase the respective stats of that Pokemon. They go up to &l31&r max."
	]
	quest.287C8B67D59F106A.title: "IV Candies"
	quest.28AE2A7C6E839EAA.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2Vivillons&r&r come with many different &owing patterns&r, 18 of them, in fact! Each unique pattern will earn you &eMalgold&r! Some wing patterns have &ospecial requirements&r. Make sure to look it up!"
		""
		"Be sure to organize them in your PC and send a &lscreenshot&r to Fid at the end of the event."
	]
	quest.28AE2A7C6E839EAA.title: "Papillon Vivillon"
	quest.28FD18097924B62F.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Hopo and one of the following: Occa, Passho, Wacan, Rindo, Yache, Chople, Kebia, Shuca, Coba, Payapa, Tanga, Charti, Kasib, Haban, Colbur, Babiri, Chilan, or Roseli."]
	quest.28FD18097924B62F.title: "Enigma Berry"
	quest.2A10D7013FD2E94B.quest_desc: [
		"&l&nHow to Use the Backpack:&r&r"
		""
		"- Can be accessed by holding it in the Main hand and &l&4right-clicking&r&r."
		""
		"- Equippable on the back by clicking the \"Equip\" button in the backpack GUI, located on the right side just above the player's inventory slots."
		""
		"- Can be accessed when equipped by pressing a key (by default B)"
		"Curios/Trinkets/Accessories compatibility makes the backpack equippable only by placing it in the \"Back\" slot."
		""
		"- Can be placed in the world as a block, making its storage accessible via hoppers/pipes."
		""
		"- Renders on the player's back when equipped."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nTier Upgrades:&r&r"
		""
		"- Offers 5 tiers: Leather, Iron, Gold, Diamond, Netherite."
		""
		"- Each of tiers adds more storage, upgrade slots, and tool slots (Configurable for each tier)."
		""
		"- Upgrading is done at a Smithing Table: Leather + Backpack + Tier Upgrade Item."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nFunctionality Upgrades:&r&r"
		""
		"- Equippable with 11 different upgrades: Tanks, Crafting, Feeding, Magnet, Pickup, Void, Furnace and more!"
		""
		"- Use the sleeping bag without resetting the spawn point."
		""
		"- Take advantage of handy tool slots and swap between equipped tools."
		""
		"- Hose Item: a useful gadget for managing fluids in your backpack."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nOrganizing Storage:&r&r"
		""
		"Offers special functions, such as marking slots as unsortable or memorizing the stack in a slot, ensuring that your storage stays organized."
		""
		"Provides Sort, Quick Stack, and Transfer buttons to seamlessly manage items"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nBackpack Customization!&r&r"
		""
		"Choose your personal style from over 45 custom backpacks, inspired by different creatures and blocks"
		""
		"The Standard backpack can be combined with any dyes you choose in crafting to create a unique look"
	]
	quest.2ADC04D08F8914F8.quest_desc: ["Can be acquired by mutating Oran and one of the following: Cheri, Chesto, Pecha, Rawst, Aspear."]
	quest.2ADC04D08F8914F8.title: "Lum Berry"
	quest.2B2BC77C42E65ED3.title: "Aquarium Tools"
	quest.2BCBE4941658839C.title: "Legendary Banglum Tools"
	quest.2C6CEB842B6221AC.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Jungle or Swamp biomes."]
	quest.2C6CEB842B6221AC.title: "Pecha Berry"
	quest.2CA7E6463A92FB77.quest_desc: [
		"Gravestones will be left behind when you die. The Gravestone will contain all your items. It will also contain XP, but some of that XP will be lost."
		""
		"Graves will last for &l30 minutes&r and then &4break&r on their own. They will have protection from others for &l15 minutes&r."
		""
		"You can use the &n/graves&r command to see your current graves, and you'll also get a compass pointing to the last grave you created."
	]
	quest.2D6A102B494CC584.quest_desc: [
		"&l&6Midas Gold&r&r is a complex ore that can only be found in the Nether. It has a very big spawn range and you'll find it almost anywhere."
		""
		"You can make a full Midas Gold armor set (which gives Luck!), but you can also &ztransmutate&r other ores into &6normal Gold&r by smelting them with Midas Gold in a Level 2 Alloy Forge!"
		""
		"A &oMidas Gold sword&r can be smithed with Midas Gold Blocks and has &lseveral forms&r depending on how many times it has been folded. At max level, it's the most powerful sword in the game, but it'll take &lhuge dedication&r! Do you have what it takes to forge this wondrous blade? At least make sure you have a Fortune pickaxe!"
	]
	quest.2D6A102B494CC584.title: "Midas Gold"
	quest.2E808828C53DB235.quest_desc: ["This &lsmithing template&r will allow you to convert chainmail armor into the unique &l&#91A2FFOsmium Chainmail&r variant, which adds armor &otoughness&r and &oknockback dampening&r."]
	quest.2E808828C53DB235.title: "Osmium Smithing Template"
	quest.2EB4B41F358CD123.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Magost and Roseli."]
	quest.2EB4B41F358CD123.title: "Qualot Berry"
	quest.2EBB2A510D979AF5.quest_desc: ["Do we need to go into &lIron&r? Incredibly versatile metal and our first real foray into the metal age. Try to collect some and we'll make some &l&8Steel&r&r out of it."]
	quest.2EBB2A510D979AF5.title: "Iron"
	quest.2EC542209C24833E.quest_desc: ["The &lOpen Crate&r can auto-output certain items. You could send an unwanted mob drop into this barrel and then shoot it out into a lava pit as an example of usage for this block."]
	quest.2EE3078582B01400.title: "Steel Tools"
	quest.2EFC4B2890D48447.quest_desc: ["The &lPokefinder&r is a simpler form of the &oPokenav&r. If you use it, a &ominimap&r will display that shows the Pokemon present near you. You can filter out species names and even if they're shinies."]
	quest.2F64075641CC0D25.title: "Desert Temple"
	quest.2FAD919ACA8E041F.quest_desc: ["You'll want to enchant your gear to make it the best it can be. Surround it with &o15 bookshelves&r to make the best enchants!"]
	quest.2FDE62CFC93B6DC6.title: "Celestium Tools"
	quest.30134DD8ED4B2CE7.quest_desc: ["&lLure Balls&r have 4x catch rate bonus against Pokemon that you've fished up with the Poke Rod!"]
	quest.3047E229D6D551DF.title: "Mage Tower"
	quest.30FADDDC0C29B1AE.quest_desc: [
		"&l&dStarrite&r&r ore is needed to make &#B539FFStar Platinum&r and thus &zCelestium&r. It's a rare material more abundant in The End. In the Overworld, you can find it at a spawn range of Y 70-260. You'll need diamond tools for this one."
		""
		"In The End, Starrite can be found in a spawn range of Y 30-90. You need a netherite pickaxe to mine End Starrite."
	]
	quest.30FADDDC0C29B1AE.title: "Starrite"
	quest.31A670DD7E13C7DD.quest_desc: [
		"&lCopper&r can now be fashioned into numerous tools and somewhat weak armor (better than nothing!)."
		""
		"It can also be smelted with &l&7tin&r&r in an Alloy Forge to make &l&6Bronze&r&r!"
	]
	quest.31A670DD7E13C7DD.title: "Copper"
	quest.3229E372928D4BAB.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Desert, Floral, Magical, Savanna, or Spooky biomes."]
	quest.3229E372928D4BAB.title: "Payapa Berry"
	quest.322E90E99300716F.quest_desc: ["&lHearty Grains&r can be found in swamp biomes, growing in water."]
	quest.32795F8D92F82D41.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Durin and Charti."]
	quest.32795F8D92F82D41.title: "Jaboca Berry"
	quest.33A6203B1049D462.quest_desc: ["A &l&2Revival Herb&r&r is a crop that can be found growing naturally in Lush Caves. It can be used to craft certain items or used directly to fully revive a fainted Pokémon whilst reducing Friendship."]
	quest.33B2B4797F4898C0.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Forest biomes."]
	quest.33B2B4797F4898C0.title: "Razz Berry"
	quest.34292845F3793F7B.quest_desc: [
		"If you wish to enter the Shop Contest, you must have a central base. I know most everyone is going to do that eventually, so here's some simple rules:"
		""
		"- Your base must not be within &56 chunks&r of another base. This rule is waived if you are Pairing with another player."
		""
		"- Make sure to &4label your base&r, as in, put a sign somewhere so I know who it belongs to."
		""
		"- When you settle on a location, please &2inform Fidchell&r as soon as possible."
	]
	quest.344CE3D75AD4DBC6.quest_desc: ["You can actually prioritize what chests can receive certain items from your system. The first thing you need is the &lInventory Configurator&r."]
	quest.35FDF2945C4BFA75.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Touga and Colbur."]
	quest.35FDF2945C4BFA75.title: "Spelon Berry"
	quest.36961F036D113C64.quest_desc: [
		"The &lInventory Proxy&r &oextends&r the faces of the inventory you connect it to. The \"arrow\" of the proxy must be pointing to that inventory."
		""
		"An example of usage for this is by extending a chest and attaching hoppers to each proxy for more specific outputs."
	]
	quest.3850296CE3F4EBAC.quest_desc: [
		"&l&3Morkite&r&r can be found in a deeper spawn range of Y -37-32 and needs iron tools to mine."
		""
		"Morkite serves as a great &lfuel&r for your &4Alloy Forges&r. Make sure to use them! "
		""
		"Additionally, they serve as fuel for a special &oDrill&r."
	]
	quest.3850296CE3F4EBAC.title: "Morkite"
	quest.3852C2D64AF47572.title: "Adamantine Tools"
	quest.388CB860DF77CC54.quest_desc: ["Time to go for a dip! Catch me some water types. Perhaps you can try using one of those fabled Pokerods to make it a bit more fun?"]
	quest.3897AC241AA50AE5.quest_desc: ["There are numerous types of crops to find in the world. Try to collect them all, you'll need them for all the finer food recipes!"]
	quest.3897AC241AA50AE5.title: "Nature's Bounty"
	quest.39239C96E1D1DCDF.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lBanglum&r&r chunks have a higher chance of popping out when you mine &oNether Banglum ore&r. "
		""
		"With them, you can craft &l&6Legendary Banglum gear&r&r."
	]
	quest.39573DCBFCB9CC9E.quest_desc: ["You can brew a &lHyper Potion&r with Sitrus berries."]
	quest.3970B6C5BDB44F76.quest_desc: ["&lRepeat Balls&r have a 3.5x catch rate bonus on any Pokemon species you've already caught!"]
	quest.39949DAFF91B5797.quest_desc: ["The &l&2Prometheum Bouquet&r&r slowly repairs and refuels the Drill while it's in your inventory!"]
	quest.3A16CB423E481FBE.title: "Palladium Armory"
	quest.3A23D9F6C6F30F4F.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Durin and Hondew."]
	quest.3A23D9F6C6F30F4F.title: "Petaya Berry"
	quest.3A4719AE4C1CEDEC.quest_desc: ["Wanna make something even better? The &lCrafting Terminal&r will include a Crafting Grid in it. This is invaluable for big storage chains!"]
	quest.3A54E657E0BBC938.quest_desc: ["In order to switch out Pokemon in your party, you'll need to access a &lPC&r. Try making your own so you can take it wherever you go and switch on the fly!"]
	quest.3B3A1AAC2212D791.quest_desc: [
		"&l&6Palladium&r&r is a material that can be found beneath lava lakes with a spawn range of Y 13-38 and requires diamond tools to mine."
		""
		"Palladium armor has &lnatural fire protection&r and other perks relating to all things hot!"
		""
		"Palladium tools have the &6Branding&r ability, which starts a combo that heats up the opponent. Igniting the target will then cause them to take more fire damage and make it so fire will bypass fire resistance!"
		""
		"Another quirky use for them is the crafting of Palladium rails, which acts as Boost rails when they are lavalogged. You can also make a Palladium minecart which gives Fire Protection to those seated in it."
	]
	quest.3B3A1AAC2212D791.title: "Palladium"
	quest.3B4413F63C31E7B4.quest_desc: ["These berries are dropped by these Pokemon: Absol, Sableye, Deino, Scraggy, Zorua, Pancham, Impidimp, Morpeko, Nickit."]
	quest.3B4413F63C31E7B4.title: "Roseli Berry"
	quest.3BB553B2ACA7F85A.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Persim and Chesto."]
	quest.3BB553B2ACA7F85A.title: "Wiki Berry"
	quest.3C6F3E3A07705EB2.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Dripstone, Lush, Spooky, Swamp, or Taiga biomes."]
	quest.3C6F3E3A07705EB2.title: "Kasib Berry"
	quest.3CD4C3F4E9768DBF.title: "Diamond Upgrade"
	quest.3CFF9E2D23B0FE8A.quest_desc: ["To make &l&#FF2E8DCarmot&r&r tools and armor, you'll need the smithing template to use with &dKyber&r gear."]
	quest.3CFF9E2D23B0FE8A.title: "Carmot Smithing Template"
	quest.3D6FBEE914297D3C.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Magost and Tanga."]
	quest.3D6FBEE914297D3C.title: "Watmel Berry"
	quest.3DB9910609BFD0B7.title: "Durasteel Armory"
	quest.3DD42DF928E0ED04.quest_desc: [
		"Each &l&zShiny&r&r that you catch will earn you extra Malgold! Yes, they can be the same species."
		""
		"Be sure to organize them in your PC and send a &lscreenshot&r to Fid at the end of the event."
	]
	quest.3E0ABF7C1557032C.quest_desc: [
		"In an unmodified Trial Chamber, you'll wind up finding a &lTrial Key&r when you defeat a wave of enemies from a spawner."
		""
		"If you drink an &3&lOminous Potion&r&r, you'll unlock a harder version of the spawners, and will be rewarded with the &lOminous Trial Key&r."
	]
	quest.3E8B32DA3C1643F1.title: "Osmium Armory"
	quest.3EF4DBE2C17877A9.quest_desc: [
		"The &l&9PokeRod&r&r is a tool you can use to catch Pokemon in bodies of water (no matter how big or small)!"
		""
		"There are &l48&r unique PokeRods based on the Pokeball used to craft the PokeRod."
		""
		"PokeRods are obtained via a Smithing Table using any Pokeball, a Fishing Rod and a &lPokeRods Upgrade Smithing Template&r. Crafting an existing PokeRods with a different Pokeball will change the bobber to that ball."
		""
		"The Smithing Template can be found via fishing or via &oMini Dungeon Shipwreck Cove&r and &oFishing Boat&r structures. Optionally, they can be traded for via a Master Level fisherman villager."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You are able to attach different kinds of &l&6bait&r&r to your PokeRod, and they all have different effects, some examples being increasing &obite chance&r and increasing the chances of certain &oNatures&r."
		""
		"The full list of bait you can attach is quite extensive, and can be found on the Cobblemon Wiki."
	]
	quest.3EF4DBE2C17877A9.title: "Gone Fishin'"
	quest.40361C5F43AD8FFF.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Wiki and Bluk."]
	quest.40361C5F43AD8FFF.title: "Cornn Berry"
	quest.408938CBF270F690.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Forest, Mushroom, Spooky, or Swamp biomes."]
	quest.408938CBF270F690.title: "Kebia Berry"
	quest.41C2AA82BD70FAF4.quest_desc: ["The &lFishingNav&r is a Pokenav designed specifically to look up Pokemon that can be fished up with a Pokerod in the biome you're in."]
	quest.421054B9F683D551.quest_desc: ["This special &6golden sword&r can be upgraded by adding more Midas Gold blocks to it in the Smithing Table."]
	quest.425998E1E5CCE48D.quest_desc: [
		"&lAdditional Placements&r is a Vanilla-lite mod that allows you to place blocks in new orientations."
		""
		"No new items are added - instead, the placement logic of the original blocks is modified."
		""
		"Currently supports (includes most mod-added as well):"
		""
		"Slabs - allows vertical placement"
		"Stairs - allows vertical placement, and stairs will connect vertically as well"
		"Carpets - allows placement on walls and ceilings"
		"Pressure Plates - allows placement on walls and ceilings"
	]
	quest.425998E1E5CCE48D.title: "Additional Placements"
	quest.425AFEDD051584BA.quest_desc: [
		"The &lREI mod (Roughly Enough Items)&r is one of the most useful utility/QoL mods in modern modpacks — especially as a replacement or evolution of JEI."
		""
		"It's the mod that gives you all the extra interfaces when you open up your menu. Namely, it shows all the possible block entities and items you can get in the menu to the right (by default)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"With REI, you can press &4&n&lR&r&r&r while hovering over an item to view recipes that &2make it&r."
		""
		"Pressing &4&n&lU&r&r&r while hovering over an item will show you what you can make with the item!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There is a &lbookmark bar&r to the left where you can &2save item recipes&r. Just press &4&n&lA&r&r&r while hovering over an item to add it. You can then &l&4CTRL+click&r&r on that icon to automatically populate your crafting grid with the recipe items!"
		""
		"Better yet, open the recipe and &l&4SHIFT+click&r the Plus icon to put all the ingredients you have into the grid."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Lastly, &dSmart Searches&r can be done via the search bar on the &lbottom&r. You can input mod filters here. For example, if you want to find all items under the &oFarmer's Delight&r modpack, you can put in &n@farmers&r."
	]
	quest.425AFEDD051584BA.title: "(REI) Roughly Enough Items"
	quest.42CDB4057B947E30.quest_desc: [
		"The earth is packed with a plethora of &o&dminerals&r&r and &o&bores&r that can be used to your advantage. Some ores you can only find very deep down, but they produce even &ostronger tools and weapons...&r"
		""
		"You can develop a number of &l&4alloys&r&r with these ores too, making even more powerful items."
		""
		"Try to unearth all the many ores you can find in this world, and create valuable tools and dazzling armor sets!"
	]
	quest.42CDB4057B947E30.title: "Mythic Metals"
	quest.42E3C37542F46144.quest_desc: [
		"These &lenchanted&r blocks can only be obtained from bartering Midas Gold with &oPiglins&r and are required to get the Midas Gold Sword up to the &6Royal&r level. It can also be used on a certain &4Staff&r and is an upgrade for the &l&bMythril Drill&r&r."
		""
		"How did they acquire such mystical blocks of gold? Who knows? Maybe they've got a point with their exaltation of the metal..."
	]
	quest.42E501458AEDAEEF.title: "Bronze Tools"
	quest.43017C4C63774C9B.quest_desc: ["&lPolymorphic Item Filters&r only insert items that already exist in the connected inventory."]
	quest.44630AB61638D7B0.title: "Adamantine Armory"
	quest.44A1D8E8BAAE734B.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Jungle, Temperate, or Lush biomes."]
	quest.44A1D8E8BAAE734B.title: "Rindo Berry"
	quest.44B301AE0E1237BB.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Plains biomes."]
	quest.44B301AE0E1237BB.title: "Cheri Berry"
	quest.45A1CDCD5F27D605.quest_desc: [
		"Put your most frequently used items within convenient reach. &lStorage Drawers&r borrows ideas from Jabba and Bibliocraft, resulting in a highly functional, compact, and aesthetic storage solution that is meant to complement rather than replace those mods."
		""
		"There is no traditional slotted inventory with these containers. Interaction is click-based similar to Jabba. Clicking on one of drawers on front will interact with that drawer."
		""
		"&l&4Right-Click&r&r: Insert full stack in hand into drawer (or partial stack if the drawer fills)."
		"&l&4Double-Right-Click&r&r: Insert all compatible stacks in inventory into drawer (or until drawer fills)."
		"&l&4Left-Click&r&r: Remove a single item from the drawer."
		"&l&4Shift+Left-Click&r&r: Remove a full stack from the drawer."
		"&l&4Shift+Right-Click with empty hand&r&r: Open a UI to see exact item counts and manage applied upgrades."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nStorage Upgrades:&r&r"
		""
		"Capacity can be further boosted with &l&estorage upgrades&r&r. Upgrades do not need to be applied in sequence, so you can pick the size you need from the start."
		""
		"Many other kinds of upgrades can also be applied:"
		""
		"- &oBalanced Fill:&r Equalizes item counts between multiple drawers holding the same item"
		"- &oConversion:&r Can automatically substitute same-kind items, like variations of metal ingots"
		"- &oFill Level:&r Adds a visual fill bar"
		"- &oHopper:&r Collects items in-world"
		"- &oIllumination:&r Brightens labels in dark places"
		"- &oMagnet:&r Collects items in-world from a distance"
		"- &oOne Stack:&r Downgrades storage space to a single stack"
		"- &oPortability:&r Carry drawers without encumberance (if option is enabled)"
		"- &oRedstone:&r Emit redstone based on fill levels"
		"- &oVoid:&r Voids excess items added to full drawers"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nDrawer Keys:&r&r"
		""
		"Drawers can also be locked or unlocked with the &2Drawer Key&r. When a drawer is locked, it will maintain its current item association even if the last item is removed. This will prevent pipes and other transport systems from re-filling that drawer with other items."
		""
		"Other keys and tools exist to alter other aspects of drawers:"
		""
		"- &oQuantify Key:&r Adds item counts to drawers"
		"- &oConcealment Key:&r Hide drawer labels (and save render performance)"
		"- &oPriority Key:&r Change a drawer's priority on a controller network"
		"- &oPersonal Key:&r Prevent other players from interacting with your drawer blocks"
		"- &oPause Key:&r Pauses a drawer from moving items on a network or performing most actions"
		"- &oDrawer Puller:&r A tool to remove individual drawers from their blocks"
		""
		"The \"key\" tools can also be used on controllers to mass-act on all connected drawers."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nCompact Drawers:&r&r"
		""
		"&lCompacting drawers&r are a special stone-colored drawer that auto-convert compressible items. Instead of manually crafting and uncrafting between gold blocks, ingots, and nuggets, put them in a compacting drawer. The drawer will internally maintain a pool of the material, and let you insert or remove the material in any of the shown forms."
		""
		"The compacting behavior applies to any item with a compressed recipe, including redstone, glowstone, wheat, and many others."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nDrawer Controllers:&r&r"
		""
		"&lDrawer Controllers&r are the second special block in the mod. They will search for any connected drawer within 50 blocks by default (configurable), and then expose all of those drawers as a large combined inventory. This lets you hook up a single pipe, tube, duct, spark, storage bus, etc. and interact with the entire bank of drawers."
		""
		"The second function of the controller is as a deposit-only interactive block. By &l&4right-clicking&r&r on the front face with an item, the item will be deposited into the connected network. By &l&4double-right clicking&r&r, it will attempt to dump your entire inventory. Items will only be dumped if they already exist in the network, allowing you to clear out a bunch of mob drops or farmed crops without literally dumping your entire inventory."
	]
	quest.45A1CDCD5F27D605.title: "Storage Drawers"
	quest.469A093404E1BF33.quest_desc: ["Get in the thick of it and catch me 10 grass types!"]
	quest.469F8575C92FFD0F.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Watmel and Chilan."]
	quest.469F8575C92FFD0F.title: "Custap Berry"
	quest.46EF6F3A1A91BAAC.quest_desc: [
		"The &l&6Banglum Smithing Template&r&r is needed to create Legendary Banglum gear!"
		""
		"The Legendary Banglum pickaxe and shovel have the &lBlast Mining&r perk. By right clicking harder blocks with the pickaxe, you can mine a 3x3x6 space! It does take a lot of durability, so be wary."
	]
	quest.46EF6F3A1A91BAAC.title: "Banglum Smithing"
	quest.4734447283D34FC3.quest_desc: ["In every &lOcean Monument&r, there are &l&3Elder Guardians&r&r swimming about inside the structure. Slay them and be rewarded! Just be aware of that nasty &4Mining Fatigue&r curse!"]
	quest.477D5B1CF68B0EB6.title: "Prometheum Tools"
	quest.479D62D4C227BB42.title: "Runite Tools"
	quest.47CA4C7A77DFC58C.title: "Copper Armory"
	quest.47EFD4C82548F56C.quest_desc: ["It's certainly ice to meet these chilly Pokemon. Catch me 10 of them!"]
	quest.47FCB704056FE9BE.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Arid biomes."]
	quest.47FCB704056FE9BE.title: "Pinap Berry"
	quest.48AEE0A118A59732.quest_desc: ["Get all three frog variants on a leash! Ribbit!"]
	quest.490A8C9D363A2BDE.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Freezing or Taiga biomes."]
	quest.490A8C9D363A2BDE.title: "Yache Berry"
	quest.49204AF914998F69.quest_desc: ["&lDive Balls&r have a 3.5x catch rate bonus vs Pokemon that are submerged in water."]
	quest.49457C9E62C6CAD9.title: "Tidesinger Tools"
	quest.495B4CAEBB92D461.quest_desc: [
		"The &l&6Bullet Pepper&r&r is a vegetable that can be found in &4Crimson Forests&r in the Nether. They grow on &lPowdery Cannon&r (what look like black bamboo) and can be chopped off the top with a sword or an axe."
		""
		"You can plant Bullet Peppers on Netherrack. Powdery Cannons can also be grown and can serve as bamboo replacements."
		""
		"To safely harvest them without a mini explosion, right click with a knife."
	]
	quest.497D901B898AAE03.title: "Iron Upgrade"
	quest.49C712FED2F4AF8F.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Aguav and Wepear."]
	quest.49C712FED2F4AF8F.title: "Rabuta Berry"
	quest.49EB9B6B1753CA1E.title: "Orichalcum Tools"
	quest.4A06A4427DF99A4D.quest_desc: [
		"&l&6Enchanted Midas Gold&r&r blocks can be acquired by bartering &6Midas Gold&r with &oPiglins&r."
		""
		"You can use these enchanted blocks as a &lMythril Drill Upgrade&r. It will give your Drill &d+2 Luck&r, and will randomly drop &6Raw Gold&r when mining ores."
	]
	quest.4A37A30C4F2B4949.quest_desc: [
		"With some ingredients, you'll be able to cook delectable treats that can &obenefit your Pokemon&r and help you find &ostronger ones&r in the wild."
		""
		"First create a &lCampfire Pot&r and place it over a campfire."
		""
		"The 3x3 grid on the right is where you put your ingredients. The three slots on the top-right are seasoning slots, where you can place a number of edibles to enhance certain foods."
	]
	quest.4A37A30C4F2B4949.title: "Campfire Pots"
	quest.4A3A3E69D200B497.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Mountain, Bamboo, or Taiga biomes."]
	quest.4A3A3E69D200B497.title: "Chople Berry"
	quest.4A68CFCD9D4E58D0.quest_desc: ["&lDusk Balls&r have a catch rate bonus of 3.5x when the light level is 0. The bonus is 3x if the light level is 1-7. Works well in dark caves!"]
	quest.4AE4D25563362BD1.quest_desc: ["You can put Skillets on &lstove tops&r. Food will cook faster on it than if you were to cook food in your off-hand."]
	quest.4B6343D542EF8D22.title: "Bronze Armory"
	quest.4BB0D83ADDBD63C5.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Plains biomes."]
	quest.4BB0D83ADDBD63C5.title: "Wepear Berry"
	quest.4BBC23A45E9FC314.title: "Iron Tools"
	quest.4C15E35E651C9FB9.title: "Metallurgium Armory"
	quest.4CA8A45663926F28.quest_desc: [
		"&lMochis&r can increase the &zEVs&r of your Pokemon. There are several different kinds to make."
		""
		"In order to cook them, you'll need &oHearty Grains&r, &oHoney Bottles&r, and any of the &oEV-dropping berries&r (Enigma is used for Fresh-Start)."
		""
		"EVs (Effort Values) are stats that, like IVs, increase the respective stat of a Pokemon. EVs go up to &l252&r, but the total EVs they can have overall is &l&e510&r&r. The bigger your effort values are, the more gets added to a stat upon level up."
		""
		"Therefore, the most optimal time to max out EVs is on a Level 1 Pokemon."
	]
	quest.4CA8A45663926F28.title: "Mochis"
	quest.4CECE6AC63ECB7E9.title: "Stormyx Armory"
	quest.4DA93E4C1ED1D90A.quest_desc: [
		"You can now cook extra-small &lEXP candies&r! You'll need a &oSculk block&r and &oHoneycomb.&r"
		""
		"EXP candies can be &lupgraded&r to their superior forms in the Cooking Pot or a standard crafting grid."
	]
	quest.4DE8DFD3B60EF503.quest_desc: [
		"&lPoke Snacks&r are a luring item that can be placed in the world to spawn a Pokemon."
		""
		"To make these delicious snacks, put Milk, Honey Bottles, a Vivichoke, and three Hearty Grains in the Campfire Pot."
		""
		"You can put various food items in the Seasoning slots to change the spawning Pokemon's &eproperties&r. These properties are very similar to ones for &oFishing Bait&r, so check out the tooltips to see what they can do! You can type \"bait\" into the REI search bar to see all available bait."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Pokemon might sometimes be too shy if there's a lot around! Try these two things if you're not getting many bites:"
		""
		"- Place down a &lRepel block&r near the Snack. Make sure to despawn Pokemon in the area!"
		"- Putting the Snack &l48 blocks away&r from you seems to work well."
	]
	quest.4E0BBC437295EEC0.quest_desc: [
		"Once you've gathered Apricorns, you can put two colored Apricorns together with an ingot in the center to craft your &ofirst Pokeball&r!"
		""
		"Try to craft any one of the listed Pokeballs in this quest."
		""
		"Once you make it, equip it into your hand and toss it with &l&4right-click&r&r. It'll need to hit a Pokemon for you to catch it, of course."
		""
		"There are many varieties of Pokeballs with different modifiers, making it easier to catch certain Pokemon, or even having certain effects &oafter&r catching them!"
		""
		"Go out there, craft all sorts of balls, and catch as many different Pokemon as you can! &lHave fun!&r"
	]
	quest.4E0BBC437295EEC0.title: "A Monster in Your Pocket"
	quest.4EACD5B94E153DFC.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2Vivichoke&r&r is a rare item only obtained by harvesting vivichoke crops grown from vivichoke seeds. Its primary use is to increase a medicine's potency and is used in numerous recipes."
		""
		"Vivichokes are obtained by harvesting the final stage of a vivichoke crop, which produces one vivichoke."
	]
	quest.4EACEBFB386862A1.quest_desc: ["If you want a bulkier option for connecting distant inventories, you can use &l&6Inventory Trims&r&r, which functions similarly to the cables, but doesn't need an Inventory Cable Connector."]
	quest.4EE20490F5F989B8.quest_desc: ["&l&6Pokenavs&r&r are indispensible tools that will allow you to determine the Pokemon that typically populate a biome. It also aids in locating &lstronger Pokemon&r that have spawned in the area."]
	quest.4EE20490F5F989B8.title: "Finding the Right One"
	quest.4EE59B0D72B6FEE8.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have &l&2Medicinal Brews&r&r, you can make all manners of &l&bPotions&r&r."
		""
		"To make a basic one, put an &9Oran Berry&r into the Campfire Pot along with the Brews you made previously. Congratulations, you've made a real potion!"
	]
	quest.4EE59B0D72B6FEE8.title: "Potion Brewer"
	quest.4EF9B6A834492341.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Cornn and Rindo."]
	quest.4EF9B6A834492341.title: "Kelpsy Berry"
	quest.4FA651A5F77241CA.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Peak, Temperate, and Sky biomes."]
	quest.4FA651A5F77241CA.title: "Coba Berry"
	quest.4FBF2CE750FC5935.quest_desc: ["A strong stature and a steely heart! Fetch me 10 of these resilient Steel types!"]
	quest.4FD0102F8AFF2AC8.quest_desc: ["This template can be made out of &6Enchanted Midas Gold&r blocks and is needed to upgrade the Midas Gold Sword to the &l&eRoyal&r&r level."]
	quest.4FD0102F8AFF2AC8.title: "Royal Midas Gold Smithing Template"
	quest.4FD124CFD65DAAFA.quest_desc: ["Every Pokemon you can level up to &l&e100&r&r will be worth extra points! Be sure to organize them in your PC and send a &lscreenshot&r to Fid at the end of the event."]
	quest.4FD4C5290B78F14A.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Spelon and Chople."]
	quest.4FD4C5290B78F14A.title: "Lansat Berry"
	quest.4FD834CABAB50FE4.quest_desc: ["&lAncient Jet Balls&r fly further and have a 2x catch rate bonus!"]
	quest.50C4098388E143CE.quest_desc: [
		"&l&#91A2FFOsmium&r&r can be found in high places and mountain biomes. It spawns at a range of Y 50-120."
		""
		"Looking for this ore can be very difficult. When you find the right spot, you can find a lot of it. It is recommended to look around the base of mountains and close to the surface (strip mining might be the most viable method here). You don't want to mine above a large cave system that can leak into other biomes."
		""
		"I heard people found some in Meadows or Cherry Groves too..."
		""
		"The armor set has an impressive &oToughness&r and &oKnockback Reduction rating&r."
	]
	quest.50C4098388E143CE.title: "Osmium"
	quest.51C8E153C7930685.quest_desc: ["A &lMax Potion&r can be acquired by brewing &lVivichokes&r with &oHyper Potions&r."]
	quest.51D177766092504E.quest_desc: ["These evil wizards can drop a &lTotem of Undying&r. You can find them in &oWoodland Mansions&r or in &oVillage Raids&r."]
	quest.52006C4663D55A38.quest_desc: ["&lLevel Balls&r scale in effectiveness depending on your Pokemon's level compared the foe's. The higher your Pokemon's level, the better. Range is 1x to 4x."]
	quest.524D537F3B5F50AB.quest_desc: ["The &lFriend Ball&r only has a catch rate of 1x, but Pokemon caught with it get a Friendship boost of 150! Invaluable for certain species like Eevee and Riolu!"]
	quest.52FAAC2918E95D63.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Mago and Nanab."]
	quest.52FAAC2918E95D63.title: "Magost Berry"
	quest.532B84DDFECDA704.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Jungle or Swamp biomes."]
	quest.532B84DDFECDA704.title: "Nanab Berry"
	quest.534523C7AE253715.quest_desc: ["A &lMedicinal Brew&r along with either a Figy/Iapapa/Wiki/Hondew/Mago berry is needed to brew this better potion."]
	quest.539DFB0EB0890899.quest_desc: ["You all know it, you all love it. The &lMaster Ball&r is a guaranteed capture of any Pokemon."]
	quest.53CE90F279E983F1.quest_desc: ["These Pokemon are blazing hot! If you can take the heat, see if you can manage to catch me 10 of them."]
	quest.54016F053A038BB4.quest_desc: [
		"The &l&2Cutting Board&r&r lets you slice things in order to use them in recipes for finer foods."
		""
		"Once you make one, lay it down, place a piece of meat on it, then &l&4right-click&r&r it with a knife."
	]
	quest.55066B3850AF8632.quest_desc: ["All quests that have a diamond-shaped slot, excluding this one, will earn you &l&eMalgold&r&r at the conclusion of the event!"]
	quest.5517C0DE9EA8E792.quest_desc: [
		"Looking to be a real warrior of the sea?"
		""
		"Once you have &l&#5EA3FFAquarium&r and a handful of coral, you can create the &lTidesinger Smithing Template&r."
		""
		"You can apply this to your Aquarium tools and armor to boost them further. In addition, depending on the coral you use, your armor can &ochange appearance&r!"
	]
	quest.5517C0DE9EA8E792.title: "Tidesinger Smithing Template"
	quest.55561CB5C75441AB.quest_desc: [
		"The &l&4Carmot Stone&r&r can be found rarely when mining Carmot ore."
		""
		"This special stone can be attached to the &lMythril Drill&r and will give it &z+1 Fortune&r, which even goes over the normal limit of Fortune III!"
	]
	quest.55E8B44C5CC60B34.quest_desc: ["Don't bug me! Instead, bring me 10 Bug Types!"]
	quest.55EBE3847A6C0487.title: "Banglum Tools"
	quest.56396D79C830E10E.quest_desc: [
		"&l&5Manganese&r&r can be found in a peculiar spawn range of Y 28-48."
		""
		"If you can locate this ore, we can mix it into two different alloys: &l&8Steel&r&r and &l&0Durasteel&r&r&r."
	]
	quest.56396D79C830E10E.title: "Manganese"
	quest.566AC4ECD5227CB1.quest_desc: [
		"&l&4Nether Wart&r&r can be found in the Nether, usually in Fortresses and sometimes in Bastions."
		""
		"They are a vital ingredient in the production of &lpotions&r in a &oBrewing Stand&r."
	]
	quest.567E56EAA743CD88.title: "Celestium Armory"
	quest.56C75098203420E0.quest_desc: [
		"&l&#5EA3FFAquarium Ore&r&r&r is an ore that can be mostly found in water biomes, spawning at a range of Y 21-69. They need iron tools to mine."
		""
		"The armor you can craft from this ore has perks that will help your underwater expeditions greatly!"
	]
	quest.56C75098203420E0.title: "Aquarium"
	quest.57030002A111F614.quest_desc: ["This template is needed to create &zCelestium&r and &zMetallurgium&r equipment."]
	quest.57030002A111F614.title: "Unobtainium Alloy Upgrade"
	quest.5733BB554AFE9F89.quest_desc: ["You get &l&8Steel&r&r by smelting &oIron&r with &oManganese&r. While it doesn't quite reach the level of Diamonds still, the armor set does have Toughness, albeit a small amount."]
	quest.574A2AD94C499F95.quest_desc: [
		"&lTin&r is an early-game ore that can be found at Y 64-92. They require stone tools to mine."
		""
		"On its own, Tin doesn't do much, but smelt it in a Forge multiblock with Copper to get &l&6Bronze&r&r!"
	]
	quest.574A2AD94C499F95.title: "Tin"
	quest.57672C38FC79B286.quest_desc: [
		"By folding a Gilded Midas Sword &6640 times&r, you are now ready to reach the &l&eRoyal&r&r level. Use a Royal Midas Gold Smithing Template to transform your sword into a Royal Midas Gold Sword, which adds in the &6Midas Touch&r perk. This will get you more Midas Gold when killing entities. As if you need more!!"
		""
		"Folding the sword this many times also makes it the &lmost powerful sword&r in the game. Congrats!"
	]
	quest.57C3C4FD849ABE9E.title: "Stormyx Tools"
	quest.5810305CFD31558B.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2Farmer's Delight&r&r is a mod that gently expands upon farming and cooking in Minecraft."
		""
		"Using a simple cooking system and a few familiar ingredients, you'll be able to prepare a wide variety of hearty meals: from sandwiches to salads and stews, from beautiful desserts to mouth-watering feasts, no ingredient will be left behind in your kitchen!"
		""
		"It also introduces a &orich set of utilities&r: a way to improve the very soil your crops grow in, a brand new kind of tool to scavenge resources with, cute decorations for your builds, and many blocks and items to help you on your adventure!"
		""
		"It's time to farm a little bit of everything!"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nGetting started:&r&r"
		""
		"The Advancements tab for this modpack will explain all its different aspects."
		""
		"If you want a more direct way to get started, first get a &l&2Knife&r&r. Knives are scavenging tools: they allow you to obtain a few more resources from both fauna and flora."
		""
		"Any animals you slay using a Knife are &oguaranteed&r to drop secondary items, such as &4Leather&r and &4Feathers&r;"
		""
		"Grassy plants (grass, wheat, rice etc) cut with a Knife will occasionally yield &4Straw&r, a firm and useful fiber;"
		""
		"They act as a modest &omelee weapon&r: swings faster than a sword for lesser damage;"
		""
		"Later on, they are also useful for &lcutting and portioning&r ingredients when preparing meals."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nStraw and Rope:&r&r"
		""
		"Using a Knife on grassy plants will yield &4Straw&r, a useful building and composting material. Early on, it's best used to craft some &lRopes&r."
		""
		"&4Ropes&r are essentially &oreverse scaffolding&r: the can be continuously deployed downward from the same spot, and can be climbed without collision. This allows players to safely descend or ascend high altitudes, such as ravines or mountains."
		""
		"Ropes can also be crafted into a few things:"
		""
		"5 Ropes can be tied into a single &4Lead&r, to help you corral animals early on;"
		""
		"A 2x2 of Ropes can be crafted into a &4Safety Net&r, a block that fully absorbs your fall without dealing damage."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nWild Crops:&r&r"
		""
		"When exploring, keep an eye out for certain flowering plants. All crops, from both this mod and vanilla, now spawn in nature as &4Wild Crops&r. These wild variants are rather rough, and not very suitable for eating, so you'll only be able to forage one sample or seed out of them. However, this might be more than enough to kickstart a humble farm once you settle down somewhere."
		""
		"Each wild crop depends on certain biomes or temperatures, so make sure to cover as many places as you can!"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nBenefits:&r&r"
		""
		"Some foods can give you a boost in another way: through &ebeneficial effects&r!"
		""
		"- &oComfort:&r Allows the player to maintain natural regeneration even if they're too hungry to do so normally. This is indicated by a silver sheen scrolling over the health meter."
		""
		"- &oNourishment:&r Nourishment prevents players from losing hunger or saturation through exhausting actions, such as running, jumping and attacking mobs. This effectively extends the hunger bar beyond its saturation limit, delaying the time before players need to eat again."
		""
		"- &oPungent:&r Subtracts a percentage of your hearts but prevents you from burning out- if you have fire protection armor or the fire resistance effect you regenerate when near heat sources."
		""
		"- &oPoaching:&r A new Enchantment/Cursed for Axes/Swords that allows you to get Farmer's Delight ingredients without the Knife! Be careful when choosing your prey or you might get a scare..."
	]
	quest.5810305CFD31558B.title: "Farmer's Delight"
	quest.586DCEE78D6E3148.title: "Palladium Tools"
	quest.59141C2A0FDA2FCB.quest_desc: [
		"The &#5EA3FF&lAquarium Pearl&r is a Mythril Drill Upgrade that can be found rarely when mining Aquarium ore."
		""
		"When attached to the drill, it will provide the equivalent of &bAqua Affinity&r to it, which allows it to mine at a high speed even when in water."
	]
	quest.593A78F7B8B5EC9F.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Enigma and Wacan."]
	quest.593A78F7B8B5EC9F.title: "Maranga Berry"
	quest.5953EB91EF1E7A25.quest_desc: ["This &lsmithing template&r is needed to upgrade the &6Midas Gold sword&r, along with a Midas Gold Block."]
	quest.5953EB91EF1E7A25.title: "Midas Gold Smithing Template"
	quest.5966E63DD3FB0E7D.quest_desc: ["This &lsmithing template&r is needed to upgrade a Mythril pickaxe into a full-fledged &#214EFF&lMythril Drill&r! You'll also need a &0&lDurasteel engine&r&r."]
	quest.5966E63DD3FB0E7D.title: "Mythril Smithing Template"
	quest.59CB8DFD30DB5D11.quest_desc: [
		"&l&nBetter Climbing:&r&r"
		""
		"- Lets you fall down ladders faster by looking down."
		""
		"- Increases upwards climb speed."
		""
		"- Up/down climbing speed gradually increases over 3 seconds."
		""
		"- Prevents the \"bump\" you sometimes get when walking into a ladder shaft to climb down."
		""
		"- Makes you not slow down when walking through a climbable block (including blocks like vines)."
		""
		"- Makes you able to jump while standing in a climbable block."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nCrawl:&r&r"
		""
		"Allows you to crawl, letting you get under 1x1 spaces. Be sure to bind it in the Controls menu!"
	]
	quest.5A010B59F037B541.title: "Hallowed Armory"
	quest.5A531AD45D44BE59.title: "Kyber Tools"
	quest.5AB80B4C369ADCD6.quest_desc: ["&lDream Balls&r have a 4x catch rate bonus vs sleeping Pokemon!"]
	quest.5B81D15BC326DD71.quest_desc: ["&lNet Balls&r are 3x as effective in catching Water or Bug types!"]
	quest.5C074400BC8C7596.title: "Metallurgium Tools"
	quest.5C7A068B0186B9A3.quest_desc: [
		"&oTom's Simple Storage&r adds a way to connect your inventories together to access them in a &lcentral terminal&r!"
		""
		"It says \"simple\" in the title, but some may find it rather complex. Follow this questline and you'll become familiar in no time!"
		""
		"First, get yourself a chest, then make a &l&6Storage Terminal&r&r, which will serve as the heart of the system."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Try attaching your new &lStorage Terminal&r to any of your chests. Interact with it and you'll see everything in that chest in the Terminal UI!"
		""
		"There's, of course, more you can do with this, so continue on with the quest!"
	]
	quest.5C7A068B0186B9A3.title: "Tom's Simple Storage"
	quest.5CAEF10E7B654694.quest_desc: [
		"&lPokémon: Magikarp Jump Forms&r are forms based on the &nPokémon: Magikarp Jump&r mobile video game, which included a variety of unique patterns for Magikarp."
		""
		"These patterns are only obtainable via fishing with a Poké Rod and are all obtainable from any biome, but have &oincreased chances&r for certain patterns in certain biomes."
		""
		"All patterns are a flat 5% chance to fish up with any level of Lure, with Luck Of The Sea boosting that chance by 2.5% per level for a max chance of 12.5%."
	]
	quest.5CE10F103922E538.quest_desc: [
		"&lSniffer Eggs&r can be recovered in Suspicious Sand or Gravel found in &oWarm Ocean ruins&r."
		""
		"To help it hatch, simply set it down on a block. It'll hatch faster on a Moss block."
		""
		"A Sniffer can find &2Torchflower&r and &2Pitcher Plant&r seeds in dirt-like blocks like podzol, mud, etc."
	]
	quest.5D0BADC51F4093A2.quest_desc: ["&lSafari balls&r have a 1.5x catch rate bonus when used outside of battle. Pretty good vs more common Pokemon species."]
	quest.5D3C45CE81FDA629.quest_desc: ["&lSaccharine Trees&r are a great source of honey if you don't want to deal with bees outright. Their leaves produce this nectar, and you can even &2slather it on the logs&r to possibly attract a Pokemon with a &lHidden Ability&r!"]
	quest.5D7A69FB5D7F7CFB.quest_desc: [
		"&lArmor trims&r let you add decorative accents to your armor. There are many kinds strewn all around the world and in structures. Find them all and get some &eMalgold&r!"
		""
		"To apply armor trims, you'll need to do it in a &lsmithing table&r with the armor piece, trim, and another ingredient unique to that armor. Make sure to refer to the \"recipe\" in EMI!"
	]
	quest.5E8FD7AA6E6F8DA7.quest_desc: ["Don't get spooked too hard as you hunt for 10 Ghost types!"]
	quest.5F1B554AB5F97566.quest_desc: ["Mischief and darkness incarnate! Locate 10 Dark types, and try not to fall to their malice!"]
	quest.5F915502518388F2.quest_desc: ["The &lLevel Emitter&r sends out a &credstone signal&r upon certain conditions in your connected inventories."]
	quest.617F2CB54F0CEF2E.quest_desc: [
		"You have a small chance of getting an &l&2Apricorn Sprout&r&r upon harvesting an Apricorn. You can plant these like any old sapling and get an Apricorn tree with that particular color."
		""
		"You can also put the Sprout &odirectly&r on Apricorn leaves for a more compact setup."
	]
	quest.617F2CB54F0CEF2E.title: "Reforestation"
	quest.61812A9F09F098A3.quest_desc: ["Toxicity runs rampant! Stop the infection and catch me 10 Poison types!"]
	quest.61B2CD3A5A226430.quest_desc: ["&l&0Wither Skeleton Skulls&r&r are a very rare drop from &oWither Skeletons&r, which can be found in Fortresses. Getting three of them and planting them atop Soul Sand formed into a T-shape will spawn the &lWither&r."]
	quest.61B2CD3A5A226430.title: "Wither Skulls"
	quest.628C44B0A42DD009.quest_desc: ["To heal &lall&r of your Pokemon's health on revival, make a &l&eMax Revive&r&r! You'll need to cook &otwo Revives&r and a &oVivichoke&r together."]
	quest.62E0FCD91B5FC2F8.quest_desc: [
		"&l&0Unobtainium&r&r is a ludicrously rare ore. Celebrate when you find some of this! It is found in a spawn range of Y -54-5 and requires Netherite tools to mine."
		""
		"This reality-bending ore is vital in the creation of &zCelestium&r and &zMetallurgium&r."
	]
	quest.62E0FCD91B5FC2F8.title: "Unobtainium"
	quest.633F6880080E6EFE.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Persim and Aspear."]
	quest.633F6880080E6EFE.title: "Iapapa Berry"
	quest.6370181906450BF7.quest_desc: ["&lGreat Balls&r have a catch rate of 1.5x compared to basic Pokeballs."]
	quest.63DFCFF26BC8C109.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2Universal Shops&r&r is a trade shop mod designed to be flexible and usable in many types of servers. It includes a craftable Trade Shop block for players!"
		""
		"First thing you need to do (as a player) is to craft a &l&3Trade Shop block&r&r. You can do it with any 4 planks, 1 wool and 1 iron ingot."
		""
		"You then place it against any &lcontainer type block&r. After that, interact with the shop block to set up types of stock and the price."
		""
		"Stock the container with the item, and you're done!"
	]
	quest.63DFCFF26BC8C109.title: "Universal Shop"
	quest.63FBB1FB33D281DD.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.63FBB1FB33D281DD.title: "Osmium Tools"
	quest.649AE5401F463171.quest_desc: ["Cure a zombie villager of its zombie curse!"]
	quest.64BB55C73F6A7A84.quest_desc: ["&lMoon Balls&r are more effective when it's night. Not just that, but there is a range of 1x-4x catch rate bonus depending on how close the moon is to a Full Moon phase!"]
	quest.65F6A5EDBE628942.quest_desc: ["&lUltra Balls&r have a whomping 2x catch rate over regular Pokeballs!"]
	quest.65FA432FF03D981D.quest_desc: [
		"Make a huge variety of interesting block textures with the &l&4Chisel&r&r item!"
		""
		"Type &n@chisel&r into the EMI search bar on the bottom right of the inventory UI to see all the different blocks you can modify with this tool!"
	]
	quest.65FA432FF03D981D.title: "Chisel Reborn"
	quest.664B39E231875431.quest_desc: ["You won't be catching many Pokemon with a &lBeast Ball&r since there aren't any UBs around. But you'll get a nice reward for crafting it anyway!"]
	quest.66B85136478D654C.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Rabuta and Babiri."]
	quest.66B85136478D654C.title: "Durin Berry"
	quest.673FF9BE525990C2.quest_desc: ["The &lBasic Inventory Hopper&r allows you to import specific items put into an inventory it's attached to. You can filter what goes through it by right-clicking on the hopper with the item in hand."]
	quest.68110A0891761206.quest_desc: ["&6320 Midas Gold Blocks later&r... you have achieved a sword that can easily rival blades made of some of the best materials. Your dedication is paying off, but can you go even further?"]
	quest.6829D721EE9622CE.quest_desc: ["&l&#28911FPrometheum&r&r is a powerful ore that &oself-repairs&r itself! It only spawns in Jungle biomes and Lush caves at a range of Y -34-48."]
	quest.6829D721EE9622CE.title: "Prometheum"
	quest.6905A17571BFEA06.quest_desc: [
		"The &lFossil Analyzer&r is part of a series of 3 blocks needed to assemble the &zRestoration Machine&r. Put all three in the same formation as shown in the quest bubbles, with the Restoration Tank on the right and the Analyzer and Data Monitor stacked on each other."
		""
		"The Fossil Analyzer is used to hold the fossils that are to be revived in the machine."
	]
	quest.6932BF2D881AB25A.title: "Osmium Chainmail Set"
	quest.6A007E0932BF7BB3.quest_desc: ["Want to be even &omore specific&r? You can use this filter and type in an &litem NBT tag&r for a certain item in a group of items."]
	quest.6A5524BD5220ED6B.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Spelon and Tamato."]
	quest.6A5524BD5220ED6B.title: "Salac Berry"
	quest.6A74055A884F0DCA.quest_desc: [
		"Want some more potent healing for your Pokemon? Try making &epotions&r! You can use a Campfire Pot to create a &l&dMedicinal Brew&r&r to start off."
		""
		"Use &l&2Medicinal Leeks&r&r and &lGlass Bottles&r to create the Medicinal Brew."
	]
	quest.6A91BC1010C7936F.title: "Quadrillum Armory"
	quest.6AE7A2951F63ED40.quest_desc: [
		"The &lSkillet&r lets you easily cook food on the go. Just hold uncooked food in your off-hand, stand near a heat source, and hold &4RMB&r."
		""
		"Alternatively, you can put it on a stove by sneaking and pressing RMB on the stove top."
	]
	quest.6B45FA1DB22C4DCA.quest_desc: [
		"The &lLevel 3 Forge&r isn't required to make even the strongest metals, but it does give greater fuel capacity, faster processing, and twice the Netherite!"
		""
		"You can make it out of Adamantine or End Stone."
	]
	quest.6B45FA1DB22C4DCA.title: "Level 3 Forge"
	quest.6D02177400DBE6CC.quest_desc: [
		"The &#214EFF&lMythril Drill&r&r is a special &oupgradable&r pickaxe. The various upgrades have a variety of different effects. When it's active, it gets &o+1 Efficiency&r."
		""
		"It needs &3Morkite&r as fuel, so make sure you get plenty of it."
		""
		"Additionally, the drill has only &ltwo&r Upgrade slots, so pick your upgrades wisely!"
	]
	quest.6D3E00537316121B.quest_desc: [
		"&lSaddles&r, unfortunately, cannot be crafted. You must find them in &l&etreasure chests&r&r, and they can appear in many different structures. Once you find a saddle, find a horse that speaks to you."
		""
		"If you can tame it, you have a truly indispensible friend for traveling on foot quickly and with ease."
	]
	quest.6E19396530552A41.quest_desc: ["Watchu need all that space for?"]
	quest.6E19396530552A41.title: "Netherite Upgrade"
	quest.6EAAC932788981BA.quest_desc: ["In addition to the farther throw distance, &lAncient Wing Balls&r have an improved catch rate bonus of 1.5x."]
	quest.6F10AF6EA0DCBA9F.quest_desc: [
		"&l&zCelestium Ingots&r&r can be created by smelting Unobtainium, Kyber, Carmot, Starrite, and Platinum in a Level 2 Alloy Forge."
		""
		"One of the strongest ores in the game, Celestium armor gives you a &b10% speed boost&r each. Additionally, Celestium can be forged with Elytras, turning them into &5Celestium Elytras&r which give more speed and rocket speed."
	]
	quest.6F10AF6EA0DCBA9F.title: "Celestium"
	quest.6F7825EA74212E00.quest_desc: [
		"&l&4Adamantine&r&r is a very tough metal that can be found deep in a spawn range of Y -54-20. You need a diamond tool to mine it."
		""
		"With Adamantine, you can create a Level 3 Forge, which isn't required to get all the mythic metals, but it does give you &ldouble&r the Netherite Ingots!"
		""
		"Adamantine can be combined with other metals to get &#FFEAB8Hallowed Ingots&r and &l&zMetallurgium&r&r."
	]
	quest.6F7825EA74212E00.title: "Adamantine"
	quest.703A47246966EAC7.quest_desc: ["Can be found in any biome."]
	quest.703A47246966EAC7.title: "Oran Berry"
	quest.70CE0DCF5D0184B9.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2Orichalcum&r&r is a powerful metal that can be found in deep regions, with a spawn range of Y -52-8 (offset by 8)."
		""
		"In addition to a great armor set that has +3 toughness, Orichalcum can be combined with other metals to get &#FFEAB8Hallowed Ingots&r and &l&zMetallurgium&r&r."
	]
	quest.70CE0DCF5D0184B9.title: "Orichalcum"
	quest.711EE3B27B91BE7E.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Pomeg and one of the following: Tamato, Kelpsy, Qualot, Hondew, or Grepa."]
	quest.711EE3B27B91BE7E.title: "Starf Berry"
	quest.7189CBDFD8D8A55C.quest_desc: [
		"You can get a &lHeavy Core&r as a rare treasure from an &lOminous Vault&r. Together with parts from a &oBreeze&r mob, you can create a &l&bMace&r&r, which has a jump attack that gets stronger the further you fall! "
		""
		"Additionally, attacking while falling will &onegate&r fall damage!"
	]
	quest.72D420416EFADC65.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Temperate or Grassland biomes."]
	quest.72D420416EFADC65.title: "Chilan Berry"
	quest.7320AF4AEB5BCC00.quest_desc: [
		"&lPokeballs&r are needed to catch and tame &owild Pokemon&r. The first steps involve finding &2Apricorn&r trees and &4harvesting&r the Apricorns."
		""
		"Please proceed down the questline to go through the whole process!"
	]
	quest.742300880C4308FA.quest_desc: ["These ancient balls are made from Tumblestone. &lAncient Feather Balls&r fly further than normal Pokeballs."]
	quest.7479CB48E33AFAAE.title: "Orichalcum Armory"
	quest.7489B2ABE19D32E4.quest_desc: ["After crafting a &lMax Revive&r, you'll be able to create a &eHealing Machine&r, which can heal all of your Pokemon &ocompletely&r. You'll have to set it down first to let it charge, which can take over &o10 minutes&r."]
	quest.757810CC6BDFC410.quest_desc: [
		"The &l&dStormyx Shell&r&r is a rare drop from mining Stormyx. Good luck with this one!"
		""
		"Attaching it to your Mythril Drill will implement Banglum defusal, making Banglum much less likely to explode."
		""
		"Banglum might not be terribly useful at the point where you mine Stormyx, but we'll give you some nice coinage for your time!"
	]
	quest.75C896170EADEAD3.title: "Iron Armory"
	quest.761ED8262D24A615.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Nomel and Yache."]
	quest.761ED8262D24A615.title: "Grepa Berry"
	quest.76ED15A730D2973C.quest_desc: [
		"Each type of berry tree yields more berries when grown in the soil of its preferred biome. Depending on the berry tree, this bonus either guarantees an additional berry or gives an equal chance of yielding 1-2 additional berries."
		""
		"&l&2Mulch&r&r can be applied to Stage 0 berry trees to mimic growth in the corresponding biome, granting the bonus yield while bypassing the need to plant the berries in their preferred biome. Below is a list of mulches and the biomes they are associated with."
		""
		"- &oLoamy:&r Plains biome."
		""
		"- &oCoarse:&r Mountains/Taiga biome."
		""
		"- &oPeat:&r Forest biome."
		""
		"- &oHumid:&r Jungle/Swamp biome."
		""
		"- &oSandy:&r Arid biome."
	]
	quest.76ED15A730D2973C.title: "Mulch and You"
	quest.77A50AE70A215BA9.quest_desc: ["To smelt more powerful metals, you'll need to move to a &eLevel 2&r Forge. You can make one out of &lPrismarine&r or &lPolished Blackstone&r."]
	quest.77A50AE70A215BA9.title: "Level 2 Forge"
	quest.77B9FDBED720B646.quest_desc: [
		"A &l&2Cooking Pot&r&r is required to make food in bowls, such as soups. With &o30+ recipes&r, this is very worth making!"
		""
		"Setting one up is very simple. First lay down a campfire, then put the Cooking Pot over the fire!"
	]
	quest.78093615B70E01BC.quest_desc: [
		"&l&eAlloy Forges&r&r are needed to smelt multiple metals at once, combining them to become alloy metals. Some Forges output more than the inputted raw ore depending on the Tier and Ore being smelted."
		""
		"The Forge is a &4multiblock&r, which is a structure made of specific blocks in a specific arrangement, usually consisting of multiple layers."
		""
		"You can make an Alloy Forge out of &b7 materials&r. &oBricks, Stone Bricks, Deepslate Bricks, Prismarine, Polished Blackstone, Adamantite and End Stone.&r"
		""
		"There are &lthree tiers&r of Forges, which have higher fuel capacity and ability to create more powerful alloys."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nConstruction:&r&r"
		""
		"The specific arrangement for an Alloy Forge facing South is as follows:"
		""
		"(X = AIR, O = BLOCK, ^ = CONTROLLER)"
		""
		"&nLayer 1:&r"
		""
		"O O O"
		"O O O"
		"O O O"
		""
		"&nLayer 2:&r"
		""
		"X O X"
		"O X O"
		"X ^ X"
		""
		"&nLayer 3:&r"
		""
		"X O X"
		"O X O"
		"X O X"
		""
		"Controller blocks must be the same material as the other blocks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nForge Materials and Tiers:&r&r"
		""
		"- &oTier 1:&r Brick, Stone Brick, Deepslate Brick."
		""
		"- &oTier 2:&r Prismarine, Polished Blackstone."
		""
		"- &oTier 3:&r Adamantine, End Stone."
	]
	quest.78093615B70E01BC.title: "All About Forges"
	quest.7814D3EBC1331DB1.quest_desc: [
		"&l&#DF81FFKyber&r&r is an ore that spawns much more frequently within Calcite, which is seen in Amethyst Geodes."
		""
		"Outside of Geodes, it has a spawn range of Y 12-52 and needs iron tools at a minimum to mine."
		""
		"Geodes are located at a spawn range of Y -56-40."
		""
		"Kyber tools are special in that they can be turned into &l&4Carmot&r&r Tools and is the only way to attain those."
		""
		"Kyber is needed to make &zCelestium&r."
	]
	quest.7814D3EBC1331DB1.title: "Kyber"
	quest.782BE19DEF6F7F86.quest_desc: [
		"&l&#FF2E8DCarmot&r&r&r is an ore that can be found in a spawn range of Y -24-10 and needs iron tools to mine."
		""
		"Carmot gear first requires that you make &l&#DF81FFKyber&r gear and then smith it with a Carmot Smithing Template. Carmot tools have the &lFortune/Looting&r enchantment by default, and this can be stacked with any additional enchanting."
		""
		"Carmot is also a crucial element in the production of &zCelestium&r ingots. "
	]
	quest.782BE19DEF6F7F86.title: "Carmot"
	quest.787FA0D4A636544B.quest_desc: ["Found in Bamboo, Mountain, or Taiga biomes."]
	quest.787FA0D4A636544B.title: "Babiri Berry"
	quest.78C7C5928B4A913C.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2Trash Cans&r&r can be used to void items and fluids! Items and Fluids can be whitelisted."
		""
		"No more need for a lava pit in your home!"
	]
	quest.79163AB4D7C38BB9.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Jungle, Sandy, Thermal, or Volcanic biomes."]
	quest.79163AB4D7C38BB9.title: "Occa Berry"
	quest.793358692840FF2D.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Badlands, Spooky, or Taiga biomes."]
	quest.793358692840FF2D.title: "Colbur Berry"
	quest.799CD6A54062025F.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Persim and Rawst."]
	quest.799CD6A54062025F.title: "Aguav Berry"
	quest.79BE22D25FDF5549.title: "Shop Contest"
	quest.79C267AC4ECF867A.title: "Kyber Armory"
	quest.79FB277F4EDF61CC.quest_desc: ["You actually don't need that silly book to access your quests. I recommend setting a keybind for Open Quests, as you'll probably be referring to this alot!"]
	quest.79FB277F4EDF61CC.title: "Quick Questbook Access"
	quest.7A1F4DB9D5B32F03.title: "Mythril Armory"
	quest.7BD1E702FB72FA29.title: "Gold Upgrade"
	quest.7BF1718E65DC5C2A.quest_desc: [
		"&l&5Star Platinum&r&r is the product of smelting Platinum and Starrite, but you knew that!"
		""
		"This beautiful ore can be used to make an armor set that passively increases your attack damage."
		""
		"It is also needed to make &zCelestium&r."
	]
	quest.7BF1718E65DC5C2A.title: "Star Platinum"
	quest.7C5D5B2805A84364.quest_desc: ["With the &lPaint Kit&r in hand, &4shift+right click&r on a block whose texture you want to paint. Then &4right-click&r on a Framed block for it take up that texture!"]
	quest.7CCBCF78EA3AF667.quest_desc: [
		"&l&7Silver&r&r is a lower-tier metal that can be found in a range of Y 25-42. It needs iron tools to mine."
		""
		"Silver can be used to craft a set of armor that is not quite as good as iron, but it sure has a nice sheen to it!"
	]
	quest.7CCBCF78EA3AF667.title: "Silver"
	quest.7D50EEE453CD90E4.title: "Star Platinum Armory"
	quest.7D8CAA42C9D09355.quest_desc: ["Truly beautiful, truly majestic! Find me 10 of these precious Fairies at once!"]
	quest.7DB7BD5949AE5FCA.quest_desc: ["Can be obtained by mutating Enigma and Kasib."]
	quest.7DB7BD5949AE5FCA.title: "Kee Berry"
	quest.7DEED09660777582.quest_desc: [
		"&lItem Filters&r are needed if you want specific items to go into specific inventories, thus making use of the &opriority function&r as well."
		""
		"&4Right-click&r the air with an Item Filter in hand to set the item being filtered."
		""
		"Then &4right-click&r on an Inventory Connector with the Configurator to put in the filter and then set your priority in the same window."
	]
	quest.7E0DA256367BCA08.quest_desc: [
		"&l&dStormyx&r&r is a Nether ore that spawns in the Y 4-60 range. You need iron tools to dig it up."
		""
		"The Stormyx armor set is known to provide &5Magic Protection&r."
	]
	quest.7E0DA256367BCA08.title: "Stormyx"
	quest.7F212EBECDAC1653.quest_desc: ["One major way to get &eMalgold&r is by catching as many unique Pokemon types as you can! At the conclusion of the event, you'll show Fid a screenshot of your Pokedex and the total amount you've caught."]
	quest.7F3BC685E49C52D1.quest_desc: [
		"You might notice very quickly that you cannot level your Pokemon beyond &lLv 15&r right now."
		""
		"Until you prove your strength by defeating &4Leaders&r, your Pokemon won't grow. First acquire a Trainer Card, either from a &oTraveling Merchant&r, or by making it yourself (you'll need a name tag)."
		""
		"Then trade this card with the Traveling Merchant by choosing either of the &otwo campaign cards&r available. Eventually, you'll see an entry in your Card showing a Leader (garbled text). Your card will glow and point towards where this leader is. Find them and defeat them!"
		""
		"(Refer to the &lRadical Trainers advancement tab&r for progression. Get ready for a challenge!)"
	]
	quest.7F3BC685E49C52D1.title: "Level Caps"
	quest.7FDB28EE93D15FE3.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Coast, Freshwater, Island, or Ocean biomes."]
	quest.7FDB28EE93D15FE3.title: "Passho Berry"
	quest.7FFDA49D386576AA.quest_desc: ["Can be found in Jungle, Magical, Mountain, Sky, or Volcanic biomes."]
